<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysian Helicopter sells subsidiary.</title>
<headline>Malaysian Helicopter sells subsidiary.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysian Helicopter Services Bhd said on Friday it has agreed to sell its entire 100 percent interest in MHS Aviation Sdn Bhd to private firm DRIR Equities Sdn Bhd for 80 million ringgit in cash.</p>
<p>MHS Aviation is involved in providing helicopter transport services to the oil and gas industry.</p>
<p>MHS, which owns a 32 percent stake in Malaysia Airlines, said in a statement that the disposal would enable it to focus and concentrate on its other business.</p>
<p>The transaction is expected to be completed in the second quarter of 1997, it said.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230 8911)</p>
